#12 487.1 -- === ENABLED FEATURES ===
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_MPI_COMMUNICATION, Enables the MPI communication back-end.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This enables the MPI communication back-end which is highly recommended on multi-node systems.
#12 487.1    See the documentation of the CMake module FindMPI to control its functionality.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_MPI_COMMUNICATION CMake option.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_BINDINGS_C, Enables the native C bindings.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    preCICE provides native bindings for C, which are compiled into the library.
#12 487.1    This feature enables the compilation and installation of the bindings into the library.
#12 487.1    Note that we strongly recommend to compile with C bindings enabled for compatibility reasons.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_BINDINGS_C CMake option.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_BINDINGS_FORTRAN, Enables the native Fortran bindings.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    preCICE provides native bindings for Fortran, which are compiled into the library.
#12 487.1    This feature enables the compilation and installation of the bindings into the library.
#12 487.1    Note that we strongly recommend to compile with Fortran bindings enabled for compatibility reasons.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_BINDINGS_FORTRAN CMake option.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_BUILD_TOOLS, Build the "precice-tools" executable
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    preCICE offers in addition to the core library a variety of tools in order to check configuration
#12 487.1    files or generate xml references. The tools are compiled into an executable called "precice-tools".
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_BUILD_TOOLS CMake option.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1 -- === DISABLED FEATURES ===
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_PETSC_MAPPING, Enables the PETSc-powered radial basic function mappings.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This enables the PETSc-based variant of radial basis function mappings which can run in parallel,
#12 487.1    also across different compute nodes. This is highly recommended for large cases running in parallel.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_PETSC_MAPPING CMake option.
#12 487.1    Requires PRECICE_FEATURE_MPI_COMMUNICATION.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_KOKKOS_KERNELS_MAPPING, Enables the Kokkos and Kokkos-kernels backend which supports the usage of GPUs or OpenMP for pum-rbf mappings.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    The executor can be specified as a subtag of the mapping configuration.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_KOKKOS_KERNELS_MAPPING CMake option.
#12 487.1    Requires Kokkos-kernels and Kokkos as additional dependencies.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_GINKGO_MAPPING, Enables the Ginkgo backend which supports the usage of GPUs and OpenMP for (global) radial-basis function mappings.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    Currently, this enables radial-basis function mappings to leverage the compute power of Nvidia/AMD GPUs and OpenMP.
#12 487.1    It uses iterative solvers provided by Ginkgo or direct solvers offered by hip/cuSolver.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_GINKGO_MAPPING CMake option.
#12 487.1    Requires the Ginkgo and Kokkos as additional dependencies.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_PYTHON_ACTIONS, Enables the support for user-defined python actions.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    preCICE allows to manipulate coupling data at runtime using configurable actions.
#12 487.1    This feature enables the support for user-defined actions written in Python based on numpy.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_PYTHON_ACTIONS CMake option.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_LIBBACKTRACE_STACKTRACES, Enables libbacktrace for stacktrace generation.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    preCICE assertions are helpful during development, however, the default stacktraces may not be sufficient.
#12 487.1    This feature enables the support for libbacktrace in boost.stacktrace.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_LIBBACKTRACE_STACKTRACES CMake option.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1  * PRECICE_FEATURE_PROFILING_COMPRESSION, Enables LZMA compression of profiling data.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    preCICE profiling information can be useful, but in some cases the size of the rank files can become too large.
#12 487.1    This feature enables LZMA compression of the records with the fastest preset to reduce the output sizes.
#12 487.1    Note that this feature introduces some profiling overhead when flushing the buffered records to file.
#12 487.1 
#12 487.1    This feature can be enabled/disabled by setting the PRECICE_FEATURE_PROFILING_COMPRESSION CMake option.
#12 487.1   
#12 487.1 
